{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/pulls/89","id":5375836418,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVrr5oM8AAAABQGzBAg","html_url":"https://github.com/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/pull/89","diff_url":"https://github.com/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/pull/89.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/pull/89.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/issues/89","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/pulls/89/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/pulls/89/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/issues/89/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/physicsvigilante/conductor_sim/statuses/d843a981a2b5ba4591f1c1afd169fd49bca7083f","number":89,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"M37a: grounded-sphere wire current from Kelvin equilibria and actual radial motion","user":{"login":"physicsvigilante","id":205609681,"node_id":"U_kgDODEFa0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/205609681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante","html_url":"https://github.com/physicsvigilante","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Draft M37a — new JEE-relevant grounded-wire-current observable\n\n**Frozen charter BEFORE code:** `docs/m37a_charter.md` committed at `89dae06df53403a8fab6743ad8bdcc10fc76c514`.\n**Released base:** M36e merge `dc347251c14e449c53d51820b4481d1bfbee2cfb`, Git tree `60b4f21aa88a2031ec50c5d1e7c15a5135a7becf`, 20/20 real main-push CI passed.\n\nM37a adds **a new ideal quasistatic ground-wire current observer**, not a new 3D electrostatic solver or fake motion animation. Existing exact Kelvin ground-sphere and M13 force/energy are observed at each source position. A teacher-supplied instantaneous velocity gives only `I_sphere→ground=-q a v_radial/d²` (conventional positive-charge direction); true radial `I(t)` consumes actual M16a trajectories, verifies the full timeline against fresh M16a integration, and retains real elapsed time, energy, guard and source model. Signed induced charge `Q_sphere=-q a/d` is derived from the native physical solution. No wire resistance, EM delay, radiation or surface-contact dynamics.\n\n**Novel evidence:** independent SI force `F_r=-k q² a d/(d²-a²)²`, mechanical energy `U=-k q² a/[2(d²-a²)]`, native-position charge derivative `-dQ/dt`; positive/negative incoming/outgoing/tangential, translated and rotated geometry, permittivity, actual RK4 radial time series, near-surface guard, hostile false sign/charge/velocity/energy/time/provenance refusals. Independent stdlib JSON physics checker imports **no conductor_sim**. Dedicated Python 3.10/3.12 workflow plus full inherited CI required.\n\n**JEE fidelity:** the M36a audit lists physical p8 Multiple Correct Q21 in `02_conductors_half_size.pdf` as partial. No unreviewed claim of the problem's complete source wording/answer or numeric givens; this PR is a reusable *current observable* first. Original source page and answer need independent visual inspection in review.\n\n**DO NOT MERGE OR MARK READY** until current exact-head source CI (full Python 3.10/3.12, historical browser, real FEMM 5, new M37a physics), completed risk-scoped independent scientific evidence checks, explicit owner authorization, exact-head merge and postmerge main-push CI. Unrelated physics/solver/renderer files remain unchanged.\n\nSee [M37a charter](docs/m37a_charter.md), [design + limits](docs/m37a.md), `src/conductor_sim/grounded_sphere_wire.py`, `tests/test_m37a_grounded_wire_current.py`, `tools/m37a_ground_wire_reference.py`, and `examples/grounded_sphere_wire_current.py`.\n\n\n### Independent review history — R4 turning-event correction, not yet independently passed\n\n**Current exact candidate HEAD:** `d843a981a2b5ba4591f1c1afd169fd49bca7083f`; **native Git TREE:** `77afef9445a3ac65d228dfe029bb7c0d5b67ba10`. Production physics code, M16a integrator, FEMM, existing renderers and original PDFs remain unchanged across these targeted corrections. Only `tools/m37a_ground_wire_reference.py`, `tests/test_m37a_grounded_wire_current.py`, and `docs/m37a.md` changed since R3.\n\n- **Independent R1:** [CHANGES REQUESTED](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/pull/6) at old source `75c984aa...`; Boolean SI scalars, units and fixed conductor metadata. Its original failed evidence remains.\n- **Independent R2:** [CHANGES REQUESTED](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/pull/7) at source `adfe9098...`; original F1–F3 fixed, physics and real M16a passed, but JSON checker accepted false max drift, negative guard, impossible terminal event.\n- **Independent R3:** [CHANGES REQUESTED](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/pull/8) at source `630f6d32...`, tree `796f319e...`. The R2 99-case independent replay and 38 R3 hostile cases passed, original F4 trio fixed, genuine duration/turning/guarded cases passed. A **new invented t=0 turning event with saved v=-.05m/s** was accepted despite a local kinematic contradiction. Its red first reviewer run [#44320918820](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/actions/runs/44320918820) is preserved.\n- **Current R4 correction:** independently SI-checked saved JSON turning events require physical radial motion, an actual outward→inward velocity reversal across authentic saved samples, essentially zero instantaneous velocity for an interior coincident-sample turn, a radial distance maximum and at most one turn. Real off-grid M16a turns, true terminal guards and old F1/F2/F3/F4 evidence checks are retained. No claim that JSON alone certifies the exact off-grid turning time or independently propagates dynamics.\n- **Developer-controlled focused gates:** source-pinned M37a on both **Python 3.10 and Python 3.12: 122/122 tests passed**, plus a genuine teacher CLI output and separate stdlib Kelvin SI export checker. Historical corrected-development test-matcher red run remains red; current source tests now reach the intended physical assertion. Full current-head original Python/FEMM5/Chromium/workflow CI must independently finish green.\n- **One TARGETED R4 independent re-review pending (not another broad physics review):** [REQUEST #04](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/blob/main/projects/conductor_sim/pr-89/REQUEST-04.md) · [REVIEWER PROMPT #04](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/blob/main/projects/conductor_sim/pr-89/REVIEWER-PROMPT-04.md). Same independent reviewer may reuse their executed R2/R3 evidence and test only changed source boundary plus its novel adversarial cases.\n\n**Source fidelity:** actual workbook `02_conductors_half_size.pdf` physical page 8 Multiple Correct Q21 specifies q>0 approaching the grounded sphere at an **externally prescribed constant small speed**, answer-key options **(1),(3)**. The native M16a accelerating history is a different genuine teaching model, not a false reproduction of printed source. Teacher numbers are not source givens; no new automatically graded whole-JEE-question claim.\n\n**PR #89 remains DRAFT AND UNMERGED; R4 independent PASS is not yet reported; NO OWNER MERGE APPROVAL.** After R4 PASS and exact-head CI success, ask the owner separately. Only then `expected_head_sha`-guarded merge, exact reviewed Git-tree check and actual postmerge main-push CI.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-18T12:21:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T14:23:43Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5229c2974c13d3f7cff88ec4db88fea9f8b2c4a9","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"physicsvigilante:m37a-grounded-sphere-wire-current","ref":"m37a-grounded-sphere-wire-current","repo":{"id":1455094176,"node_id":"R_kgDOVrr5oA","name":"conductor_sim","full_name":"physicsvigilante/conductor_sim","owner":{"login":"physicsvigilante","id":205609681,"node_id":"U_kgDODEFa0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/205609681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante","html_url":"https://github.com/physicsvigilante","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"Python","visibility":"publi